/-!
# The listings did not move (KERNEL-49 (a), CODEC-35)

Path compression changes the trie's SHAPE (a node branches at the first bit its keys disagree on, and
commits that bit), not its listing: `toList` is still the entries in bit order
(`Codec.Proofs.TrieOrder.build_listing_iff`, its statement unchanged), so every listing's wire is
byte-identical. These are the plants that would go red if it were not: each pins, over `Kernel.Sim`'s
toy parameters, the bytes the PRE-compression codec wrote for one vector of `gates/codec-vectors.tsv`
(copied from the table at main a38b84b, before the trie day) and builds the same contents through the
compressed `Trie.insert`, in an order other than the listing's, so the trie the bytes come from is the
new one, shaped by the new `insAt`. One per listing the wire carries: the cells (`kernel/trie-order`
vector 1), the journal (`kernel/journal-order` 1), the refusals (`kernel/refusal-order` 1), the rows
(`kernel/row-order` 0), a whole World (`kernel/steps` 0) and a carried state (`kernel/carried` 1). The
World's and the carried state's rows are empty: the shared-stem case (keys agreeing on 280 bits, what
compression skips) is the rows pin's alone. KERNEL-50 appended the charged member to a refused leaf: the
refusals pin and the World pin are a38b84b's bytes with that member's eight bytes inserted after the
refused leaf's two counters (the member is the listed count's), and nothing else moved.
-/

